cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "team-formation: evidence-based student team formation with constraint programming"
abstract: >-
  Staff collect a short private survey, paste it and the class list into an Excel workbook, and a
  constraint programming model (Google OR-Tools CP-SAT) assigns every student to a project team. The
  criteria are optimised in strict order of priority: no lone woman or man, shared free time, the
  worst team's skill gaps, at most one non-respondent per team, skill coverage and discipline mix.
authors:
